Feature: slice-3 / login-redirect
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-3
Verified: 2026-05-28
Anchored to: docs/18 §8.1 (the `/login` bullet) + §5 R3 (origin discipline)

What was built
==============
Cross-origin 307 redirect from the marketing origin to the app
origin, so anyone hitting superwizor.ai/login (PL or EN) lands on
app.superwizor.ai/login where Firebase Auth's IndexedDB-scoped
session actually lives.

Single change: marketing-site/next.config.ts — added an async
`redirects()` returning two entries:

    /login     → https://app.superwizor.ai/login   (307, temporary)
    /en/login  → https://app.superwizor.ai/login   (307, temporary)

Permanent: false. We use 307 instead of 308 because (a) the app
origin's login route is technically still being built (Flutter Web
in Slice 5), and (b) keeping it 307 lets us redirect to a different
path or origin later without a stuck browser cache. Once Slice 5
ships and the app-side login is stable we'll flip to permanent: true.

Why a redirect and not a `<a>` link on a real /login page
=========================================================
docs/18 §5 R3 / §8.1 say:
> `/login` — a plain `<a href="https://app.superwizor.ai/login">`
> redirect to the app origin. We deliberately do **not** run the
> Firebase login flow on `superwizor.ai`.

The Navbar already carries the cross-origin `<a>`. This feature
adds the SAFETY for users who:
- Type "superwizor.ai/login" manually.
- Click a bookmarked /login URL.
- Follow an outdated link from press, docs, email signature, etc.

Without the redirect those would 404 on the marketing origin.
A `next.config.redirects()` entry runs before middleware/proxy and
incurs no JS, no extra page render, no flash of intermediate page.

How verified
============
1. `pnpm build` exit 0. Route table unchanged (redirects() doesn't
   add routes, just URL transformations at the framework edge).

2. curl smoke (captured in evidence/.../curl.log):

       /login    → status=307, location=https://app.superwizor.ai/login
       /en/login → status=307, location=https://app.superwizor.ai/login

   Following with curl -L lands on:
       final=https://app.superwizor.ai/login

3. preview_console_logs(error) returns "No console logs" — no
   client-side errors introduced.

Note on the Navbar
==================
The Navbar component still hard-codes the same destination
("https://app.superwizor.ai/login") so users with browser-level
prefetch (or those clicking before the page mounts) bypass the
redirect entirely and go straight cross-origin. Belt + braces: the
redirect catches the edge cases.

